fieldsmith 1
# === FIELDSMITH LITERATE CASE ===
# @id: A13
# @code: A13
# @category: analytic
# @level: Analytic Verification
# @title: Analytic Benchmark A13: Fastener Inclined-Plane Thread Torque Envelope [T_min, T_max] & Weibull Regression (V57)
# @subtitle: Verify Kellermann–Klein / VDI 2230 thread-plus-collar torque decomposition T = F [½ d₂ tan(ψ + ρ') + μ_b r_b] against NASA-STD-5020B, ECSS-E-ST-32-08C, and Bossard boss-tapping benchmarks plus closed-form Weibull MLE/OLS regression.
# @verification_badge: Verified by V57 · NASA/ECSS/VDI 2230 Fastener Standards · PASS (< 0.1%)
# @doc_path: docs/analytic-tests/A13-fastener-thread-torque-and-weibull.md
# @fsm_path: examples/analytic/A13-fastener-thread-torque-and-weibull.fsm
# @starter_fsm_name: a13-fastener-torque-weibull.fsm
# @verification_refs: docs/verification/V53.md
# ---
# @check: Kellermann–Klein / VDI 2230 Thread + Collar Torque Decomposition T(F) || T = F [½ d₂ tan(ψ + ρ') + μ_b r_b],   tan ρ' = μ_t / cos(α/2),   tan ψ = P / (π d₂) || Exact Algebraic Identity (T_thread + T_collar = T_total) || Exact Match across all 7 Fixing Kinds || 0.000% || ≤ 10⁻⁹
# @check: Open-Standard Qualification Benchmarks (NASA-STD-5020B M6 / ECSS M4 / Bossard M3) || F_proof = A_t (0.75 σ_y) = 14,472 N (A286 M6×1.0);   T_max > T_min Safe Window || 4 / 4 Open Standards PASS (NASA, ECSS, VDI 2230, Bossard) || 4 / 4 PASS (T_rec within [T_min, T_max]) || 0.000% || Exact
# @check: 2-Parameter Weibull Failure Distribution Linear Regression (β, η, B10, B01) || ln(−ln(1 − F(T))) = β ln T − β ln η,   T_B10 = η (−ln 0.90)^{1/β} || R² > 0.98,  T_B01 < T_B10 < η || R² = 0.996,  Exact Quantile Ordering || < 0.1% || R² ≥ 0.98
# ---
# @assert: Applied Washer-Seat Preload Resultant |F_preload| || resultant_mag || 1250.0 || 0.5% || N
# @assert: Boss Bearing von Mises Stress σ_vm || max_vm_elem || >= 15.0 || >= 15.0 || MPa
# ---
# @step: 1. Inspect the Drilled Boss & Washer Seat Preload in Setup (2) || setup
#   Open Setup (2). A Ti-6Al-4V M4 fixing clamps a PA12 enclosure boss (`boss_plate`) with `preload=1250` N on the counterbore washer seat (`washer_seat`).
# @expected:
#   The counterbore seat receives the downward clamping preload while the base is fixed.
# @step: 2. Open the Fixing Torque & Weibull Workbench or Inspect 3D Boss Stress in Results (3) || results
#   Switch to Results (3) to inspect the 3D bearing and thread-root stress in the PA12 boss, or open the Fixings & Weibull Workbench in T14 to compare the NASA-STD-5020B, ECSS-E-ST-32-08C, VDI 2230, and Bossard self-tapping torque envelopes.
# @expected:
#   3D FEA confirms finite bearing compression under the washer seat and safe boss hoop stress.
# ---
# @theory_title: Analytic Verification A13 — Helical Inclined-Plane Thread Mechanics & Weibull Reliability (V57)
# @theory_summary:
#   Derives the Kellermann–Klein torque-preload relationship on ISO 60° and self-tapping flank profiles, internal/external thread shear stripping areas (Alexander 1977), and Weibull B10/B01 quantile estimation.
# @theory_section: A13.1 Kellermann–Klein Thread Torque & Alexander Thread-Stripping Areas
# @theory_eq:
#   T_drive = F_preload [ ½ d₂ tan(ψ + ρ') + μ_b r_b ]
#   A_s,int = π d_major L_eff [ ½ + (1/√3)(d_major − d₂)/P ],   F_strip = A_s,int τ_u,substrate
# @theory_body:
#   Minimum assembly torque T_min is governed by slip/gasket sealing plus thread-forming work, while maximum torque T_max is the minimum of torsional/tensile bolt yield (von Mises combined σ_ax² + 3τ_t²), substrate thread shear stripping, and under-head bearing crush.
# ---
# @mcp: Insert M4 Fixing & Compute [T_min, T_max] Envelope via API || insert_fixing || {"kind":"self_tapping_screw","size":"M4","engagement_mm":8,"host_id":"boss_plate","fastener_material":"ti64"}
#   Call insert_fixing to auto-tap the host and return the VDI 2230 / NASA-STD-5020B torque window.
# === END LITERATE HEADER ===

name "A13 — Fastener Thread Torque & Preload Benchmark (V57)"
material pa12

box boss_plate size=(32, 24, 10) at=(0, 0, 5) round=1
cylinder pilot_hole r=2.0 h=8.5 at=(0, 0, 4.25) subtract
cylinder counterbore r=5.0 h=2.5 at=(0, 0, 9.25) subtract
cylinder screw_shank r=2.0 h=6.0 at=(0, 0, 6.0)
cylinder screw_head r=4.5 h=2.2 at=(0, 0, 9.8)
material ti64 on screw_shank
material ti64 on screw_head

region base_mount = boss_plate.nz
region washer_seat = counterbore.bottom + screw_head.top
support mount_fix base_mount fixed=xyz
load clamp_preload washer_seat preload=1250 axis=(0, 0, -1)
solve
